---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';
---

<Base title={`Terms · ${site.name}`} description={`The terms for using ${site.name}.`} path="/terms">
  <div class="container section">
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>Terms</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>
      <p class="notice">
        This is a plain-language template and has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Please review it before relying on
        it.
      </p>

      <h2>Using {site.name}</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is an app for reading PDF and EPUB files. You can use the Free plan on one device, or subscribe
        to {site.pricing.sync.name} to sync your library and reading positions across your devices.
      </p>

      <h2>Your books</h2>
      <p>
        Your books remain yours. Only add books you have the right to read and copy to your own devices. When you
        sign in, you allow us to store your library files and reading positions for the sole purpose of syncing them
        to your devices.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You can sign in with email or Google. Keep your sign-in details safe, and let us know if you think someone
        else has used your account.
      </p>

      <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
      <p>
        {site.pricing.sync.name} is billed monthly or yearly. You can cancel anytime, and your subscription stays
        active until the end of the period you have paid for. After that, you can keep reading with the Free plan.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        We work hard to keep {site.name} reliable, but it is provided “as is”. Please keep your own copies of your
        books. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for lost data or indirect damages.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change these terms, we will update this page and, for significant changes, let signed-in users know by
        email.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions? Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
